---
import LandingLayout from '../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import {
  createBreadcrumbSchema,
  createSoftwareApplicationSchema,
  productFacts,
} from '../../data/productFacts';
import { agenticFacts, agentPromptLibrary, agentSafeValidationChecklist } from '../../data/agenticFacts';

const pageUrl = new URL('blog/localcloud-for-ai-agents/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString();
const publishDate = '2026-07-02';
const quickstartPrompt = agentPromptLibrary.find((prompt) => prompt.id === 'quickstart')?.prompt ?? '';

const structuredData = [
  createSoftwareApplicationSchema(
    pageUrl,
    'LocalCloud gives AI coding agents a safe local Google Cloud target: Docker runtime, localhost SDK endpoints, raw Markdown instructions, Agent Skills, and MCP tooling boundaries.',
  ),
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: productFacts.siteUrl },
    { name: 'Blog', url: new URL('blog/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString() },
    { name: 'LocalCloud for AI Agents', url: pageUrl },
  ]),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'LocalCloud for AI Agents',
    datePublished: publishDate,
    dateModified: publishDate,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'LocalCloud' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'LocalCloud' },
    mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
    description: 'How LocalCloud turns local Google Cloud development into an agent-safe workflow with no default GCP credentials and explicit production validation boundaries.',
  },
];
---

<LandingLayout
  title="LocalCloud for AI Agents — LocalCloud Blog"
  description="How LocalCloud gives coding agents a safe local Google Cloud sandbox: one Docker container, localhost SDK endpoints, raw Markdown instructions, Agent Skills, MCP tooling, and real-GCP validation boundaries."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <article class="site-section site-section--hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow reveal">
      <span class="site-eyebrow"><span class="site-eyebrow__pulse"></span>LocalCloud Blog</span>
      <h1 class="mt-5">LocalCloud for AI Agents</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-[var(--text-3)]">Published {publishDate} · 4 min read · AI agents, GCP emulator, MCP, Agent Skills</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)] sm:text-xl">
        Coding agents are good at writing integration code. Cloud credentials are the dangerous part. LocalCloud gives those agents a local Google Cloud target they can use by default: one Docker container, standard SDKs pointed at localhost, and explicit instructions to stop instead of falling back to real Google Cloud.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/ai/agents.md">Open /ai/agents.md</a>
        <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/ai/">AI agent guide</a>
        <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/compatibility/">Compatibility</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="site-section site-section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="site-panel p-6 reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">The prompt</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">Give this to an agent</h2>
        <pre class="mt-5 whitespace-pre-wrap text-sm"><code>{quickstartPrompt}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-section">
    <div class="container container--narrow space-y-10">
      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">Problem</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">Agents need a sandbox, not your cloud account</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          A repo that uses BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Firestore, Cloud Storage, Spanner, Bigtable, or Terraform often expects a real GCP project. If an agent follows that path blindly, a local test can become a credential request, a billing event, or a mutation against shared infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          LocalCloud changes the default. The agent starts a local runtime, exports emulator environment variables, and proves one narrow SDK or Terraform path against localhost. Production validation still happens later, deliberately, against real Google Cloud after emulator variables are removed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">What changed</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">A canonical agent entry point</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          The agent-facing entry point is <a href="/ai/agents.md">/ai/agents.md</a>. It is raw Markdown so coding agents can fetch it without parsing a rendered page. The human companion page is <a href="/ai/">/ai/</a>, which explains the workflow, copy prompts, service matrix, safety boundaries, AGENTS.md template, Agent Skills package, and raw Markdown resource index.
        </p>
        <ul class="site-list mt-5">
          <li><a href="/ai/services.md">/ai/services.md</a> gives agents the service matrix and endpoint variables.</li>
          <li><a href="/ai/compatibility.md">/ai/compatibility.md</a> keeps limitations and production boundaries explicit.</li>
          <li><a href="/ai/docs.md">/ai/docs.md</a> points agents to SDK, Terraform, seed data, and console docs.</li>
          <li><a href={`${productFacts.githubUrl}/tree/main/agent-skills`}>Agent Skills</a> provide portable workflows for BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Terraform, CI sidecars, seed data, and SDK tests.</li>
          <li><a href={`${productFacts.githubUrl}/tree/main/packages/localcloud-mcp-server`}>LocalCloud MCP server</a> provides structured tools and prompts for agents that support MCP.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">How it works</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">One local loop agents can execute</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>1. Start LocalCloud</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>{agenticFacts.dockerPullCommand}\n{agenticFacts.dockerRunCommand}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>2. Export localhost SDK endpoints</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>{agenticFacts.envExportCommand}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>3. Verify readiness</h3>
            <pre class="mt-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-xs"><code>curl -fsS {agenticFacts.healthEndpoint}</code></pre>
          </article>
          <article class="site-panel min-w-0 p-5">
            <h3>4. Run the smallest local proof</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-2)]">Create one dataset, topic, bucket, document, or table through the same SDK path the project uses. If a feature is unsupported locally, document the gap instead of using real GCP as a fallback.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <span class="site-kicker">Safety model</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3">The boundaries are part of the product</h2>
        <ul class="site-list mt-5">
          {agentSafeValidationChecklist.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-[var(--text-2)]">
          LocalCloud is for development, testing, CI, and demos. It is not a production Google Cloud replacement and does not promise complete GCP parity. Use the <a href="/services/">service catalog</a> and <a href="/compatibility/">compatibility page</a> before relying on a local result, then validate release behavior against real Google Cloud.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</LandingLayout>
